 divided into three parts: Part I focuses on the basic ideas concerning how markets operate, including topics such as consumer behavior, costs of production, and the operation of what are called perfectly competitive markets.  Part II considers market power, i.e., what happens when rather than being a price taker each firm faces its own downward sloping demand curve.  Part III considers additional topics including the decision to produce or purchase an input and the role of contracts in business decision making.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026FA, 2026SU, 2025SU, 2024SU", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2937, "crseId": 372608, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "BANA", "catalogNbr": "5030", "titleShort": "Intro to Mktg & Mktg Analytics", "titleLong": "Introduction to Marketing and Marketing Analytics", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "005", "classNbr": 18942, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:00PM", "timeEnd": "04:00PM", "startDt": "10/19/2026", "endDt": "10/22/2026", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "smv64", "firstName": "Stijn", "middleName": "", "lastName": "van Osselaer"}], "pattern": "MTR", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}, {"classMtgNbr": 2, "timeStart": "01:00PM", "timeEnd": "04